list.item:
Support for the position of Cuba, which has refused to join the treaty,
                        asserting that U.S. nuclear weapons remain in Puerto Rico, the Canal Zone
                        and “and other Latin American areas”;

The fact that the Treaty contains no ban on the transportation of nuclear
                        weapons and that the United States has refused to stop sending nuclear-armed
                        vessels through the Panama Canal;

The position taken by Brazil, with which the Soviet Union disagrees as we
                        do, with respect to the Treaty’s provisions on peaceful nuclear
                        explosions;

Concern that the Treaty may deflect some Latin American states from
                        joining the NPT, which the Soviets prefer;
                        and
